  ],
  "description": "<p>We're looking for experienced software engineers to build AI coding tasks from a codebase they know well. US$1,000 per task, and you can do as many tasks as you want.</p><p>You turn a real change from a repository you know into a task that today's best AI coding models struggle with: hard for the models, but fair for a skilled engineer. Your tasks are used to measure and train AI coding models.</p><p>Remote, any location. US$1,000 per task that passes review. Minimum of one task a week, about 10 hours a week.</p><p><br /></p><p><strong>How it works</strong></p><ol class=\"i0llva i0ll5y i0lmlu\"><li><strong>Apply. </strong>Complete a short screener interview and upload your resume.</li><li><strong>Propose.</strong> Once you're selected, pick a change from a repository you know and submit a short proposal. We approve it or suggest a better candidate.</li><li><strong>Build.</strong> In our platform, set up the repository as it was before the change, then write the brief, the correct solution and the grading checks.</li><li><strong>Stress-test. </strong>Try lazy, incorrect and shortcut solutions and make sure your checks catch them.</li><li><strong>Model testing.</strong> Run your task against leading AI models until strong models often fail but a skilled engineer can clearly solve it.</li><li><strong>Review.</strong> A reviewer checks your task and you revise it. Most tasks take more than one round.</li><li><strong>Next task.</strong> Once your task is accepted, start another.</li></ol><p><br /></p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul class=\"i0llva i0ll5z i0lmlu\"><li>2+ years of professional software engineering</li><li>Code merged into a public open-source repository, ideally one you know well. A private codebase you own may also qualify (not employer or client code)</li><li>Strong in at least one of Python, TypeScript, Go, Rust, Java or C++</li><li>Solid with Docker, Linux, Git and automated testing</li><li>Regular use of an AI coding tool</li><li>Experience writing tests, rubrics or evaluation criteria, ideally for AI models</li><li>You can explain a change clearly and concisely, in your own words</li><li>At least 10 hours a week, starting now</li><li>A secure personal or work computer (no public or shared machines)</li></ul><p><br /></p><p><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul class=\"i0llva i0ll5z i0lmlu\"><li>Deep expertise in one area, such as databases, compilers, distributed systems, security or infrastructure</li><li>Experience building agent tasks or RL environments</li></ul><p><br /></p><p><strong>Terms</strong></p><ul class=\"i0llva i0ll5z i0lmlu\"><li>US$1,000 for each task that passes our quality review, paid directly to you</li><li>Once your proposal is qualified, you sign Askable's contract and accept its terms</li><li>The work is used for AI training. The change and your solution must be your own, and you must be free to license them to us</li><li>Don't publish the work anywhere: no public pull request or public fork</li></ul><p><br /></p><p>Apply at https://www.askable.com/experts/roles/senior-software-engineer</p><br/><br/>Please mention the word **LEVITY** and tag RMTAzLjEyMS4xMi4xODU= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMTAzLjEyMS4xMi4xODU=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.",
